```python
    @property
    def alias(self) -> str:
        if self.mode == "validation":
            a = self.field_info.validation_alias
            if not isinstance(a, str):
                a = self.field_info.alias
        else:
            a = self.field_info.serialization_alias
            if not isinstance(a, str):
                a = self.field_info.alias
        return a if a is not None else self.name
```

Then for `AliasPath`, `isinstance(a, str)` will be `False`, so it will use `self.field_info.alias`, which is `None` (since only `validation_alias` was set), and then it will return `self.name` which is `foo`. This matches the "only string value is currently supported" requirement.

